/*!
\page page_steventinfo StEventInfo

\brief Per-event metadata: run/event numbers, timestamp, L0 trigger mask, RHIC bunch-crossing ID, event size.

\section steventinfo_overview Overview
\c StEventInfo stores the identifying metadata for a single recorded collision event.
It provides the run number, event number, Unix timestamp, the L0 hardware trigger bitmask,
the 64-bit RHIC bunch-crossing identifier (stored as two 32-bit words), and the raw event
size in bytes.  It is the first place to look when selecting specific trigger conditions,
labelling histograms, or performing run-quality checks.

\section steventinfo_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code
TObject
 └── StObject
      └── StEventInfo
\endcode

\section steventinfo_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| TString | mType | Event-type string (e.g. "physics", "laser", "pedestal") |
| Int_t | mRunId | Run number |
| Int_t | mId | Event number within the run |
| Int_t | mTime | Unix timestamp of the event trigger |
| UInt_t | mTriggerMask | Bitmask of fired L0 triggers |
| UInt_t[2] | mBunchCrossingNumber | 64-bit RHIC bunch-crossing ID: [0]=lower 32 bits, [1]=upper 32 bits |
| UInt_t | mEventSize | Raw event size in bytes |

\section steventinfo_methods Key Methods

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| `const char* type() const` | Event-type string |
| `int id() const` | Event number within the run |
| `int runId() const` | Run number |
| `int time() const` | Unix timestamp |
| `unsigned int triggerMask() const` | L0 trigger bitmask |
| `unsigned int bunchCrossingNumber(unsigned int idx) const` | Lower (idx=0) or upper (idx=1) half of 64-bit bunch-crossing ID |
| `unsigned int eventSize() const` | Raw event size in bytes |

\section steventinfo_usage Usage Example
\code{.cpp}
StEvent* event = static_cast<StEvent*>(GetInputDS("StEvent"));
StEventInfo* info = event->info();
cout << "Run: " << info->runId() << "  Event: " << info->id() << endl;
cout << "Trigger mask: 0x" << hex << info->triggerMask() << dec << endl;
unsigned long long bcid =
    (unsigned long long)info->bunchCrossingNumber(1) << 32 | info->bunchCrossingNumber(0);
\endcode

\see \ref page_struninfo
\see \ref page_steventsummary
*/
